  "notes": "Sarawak Oil Palms Berhad — integrated upstream (plantations) + downstream (refinery, kernel crushing, biodiesel). ~85,000 ha (~210,000 acres) planted in Sarawak, Malaysia. Calendar fiscal year (Dec 31). Quarterly figures from Bursa Malaysia Form 8 quarterly reports filed via SOP IR page; annual data from 2020-2024 annual reports (5-year financial summary tables). Acres derived from disclosed planted hectares × 2.47 ÷ 1000. Segments per IFRS 8 disclosure: Plantation (FFB + CPO + PK) and Downstream (refined oil, kernel oil, biodiesel). Net debt computed as borrowings − cash & equivalents. Property book = property, plant & equipment + biological assets at carrying value. Quarterly EBITDA approximated as PBT + finance costs + depreciation/amortization where disclosed; some quarterly EBITDA values are estimates triangulated from annual EBITDA and quarterly PBT trends. Pre-2020 annual data (FY2000-FY2019) compiled from SOP historical annual reports archived on Bursa Malaysia and SOP IR site — these older years are upstream-only (downstream refinery commissioned 2010-2012) so revenueBySegmentMM segments only appear post-2012; planted hectarage grew progressively from ~25k ha in early 2000s to current ~85k ha through Sarawak NCR-land plantings. Pre-refinery years had much smaller revenue and capex profile.",
